[{"q":"If you are in danger, tell a ____ adult.","options":["unknown online only","trusted","nobody","a stray animal"],"answer":1,"explain":"Parents, teachers and police can help."},{"q":"The assembly point is where we ____ in an emergency.","options":["hide from teachers","buy snacks","meet","play football first"],"answer":2,"explain":"Schools have assembly points."},{"q":"In a fire, ____ to the nearest exit.","options":["hide under a nylon bag","go back for toys first always","move quickly and calmly","use the lift in a burning house if told never"],"answer":2,"explain":"Know the escape route. Don’t use lifts in a fire."},{"q":"In a stampede, move ____ the crowd if you can, protect your chest.","options":["by sitting in the middle","sideways out of","against blindly","deeper into"],"answer":1,"explain":"Protect yourself; don’t push."},{"q":"When cycling, wear a ____.","options":["blindfold","helmet","long loose scarf in the wheel","earphones at full volume always"],"answer":1,"explain":"Helmets protect the head."},{"q":"A whistle can be used to ____ for help.","options":["iron","sweep","cook","call"],"answer":3,"explain":"Loud signals attract attention."},{"q":"Do not put ____ in sockets.","options":["the plug of a safe appliance","a charger the right way","nothing always including plugs","fingers or metal"],"answer":3,"explain":"Electric shock is dangerous."},{"q":"When crossing the road, look ____, right and left again.","options":["at your phone only","left","at the sky only","backwards only"],"answer":1,"explain":"Stop, look and listen."},{"q":"Cyber predators may pretend to be ____.","options":["the school bell","your parent at home","your head teacher in person","children or friends"],"answer":3,"explain":"Never meet an online stranger alone."},{"q":"Do not take gifts from ____.","options":["your teacher as a prize","your parents","grandparents","strangers"],"answer":3,"explain":"Strangers may not be safe."},{"q":"Flood safety: do not walk in ____ water.","o